  "executive_briefing": "The global tax landscape in 2026 is heavily shaped by the ongoing operationalization of the OECD Pillar Two 15% global minimum tax across over 140 jurisdictions, as detailed in the newly released 2026 OECD Corporate Tax Statistics. Investment hubs like Singapore and ASEAN-6 nations are adapting by introducing targeted corporate income tax rebates and grants to sustain foreign direct investment. Concurrently, tax authorities are aggressively scaling up digital compliance via continuous transaction controls and mandatory e-invoicing networks such as Singapore's InvoiceNow. Meanwhile, the international trade environment remains highly volatile due to ongoing tariff escalations and bilateral negotiations.",
